{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/170076-gun-fu","id":170076,"title":"Gun Fu","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-06-15T13:39:39-07:00","id":170076,"title":"Gun Fu","content":"The only thing Demon us missing is Gun Fu. How can I add Gun Fu to my upcoming GMC? Also it seems that Demons aren't particularly damage proof. The don't resist damage in any way and have no easy way to heal it. I'm looking for generic hacks that could ply to the splat as a whole rather than specific exploits and embeds. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T19:13:43-07:00","id":170321,"title":"","content":"Before you start &quot;Hacking&quot; demon. I suggest you try running it in the raw. Demon's are pretty powerful even starting character's have reality altering abilities that can make a storyteller chuck their notes to the side and just &quot;wing it&quot;. And if you give Demon's all these extra abilities generically you're likely going to just nullify a about half a dozen embeds and exploits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-15T23:49:09-07:00","id":170454,"title":"","content":"Or you could just give an embed or two for free, which gives the stuff you want. (The Gunman one.. and something else)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T00:06:09-07:00","id":170458,"title":"","content":"Hmm, adapting hacks for other splats I'd have these suggestions:<br /> <br /> Pain is an illusion: Since their bodies are really just constructs, demons don't suffer from wound penalties.<br /> <br /> Demonic defense: In demon form the demon uses the best of either wits or dexterity to add to defense.<br /> <br /> Quantum uncertainty: As a reflexive action a demon can spend one aether to add their primium rating to their defense until the end of the turn.<br /> <br /> As for healing, they do heal whenever they assume demon form, so while not convenient it is easy.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T11:15:28-07:00","id":170901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PencilBoy99</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/170076-gun-fu#post170076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing Demon us missing is Gun Fu. How can I add Gun Fu to my upcoming GMC? Also it seems that Demons aren't particularly damage proof. The don't resist damage in any way and have no easy way to heal it. I'm looking for generic hacks that could ply to the splat as a whole rather than specific exploits and embeds. Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div> ....<br /> <br /> Demons have armor and healing powers they get from Demonic Form you can pick. There's a rather powerful Embed that reduces all damage you take from an attack to 1 damage. There's Break To Heal. You want a demon that's damage proof? Then build it. There's lots of options out there already.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for &quot;Gun Fu?&quot; There's Merciless Gunman, Backdrop, Hellfire, any number of skill boosting abilities, option to start with a gun as part of your demon form, several other helpful demon form abilities, and the ability to make a gun into a gadget. What more do you want for gun powers? Explosions? Add in Combustion! Trick shots? You already can get a ton of bonuses - ask your ST what the penalty to do something is, then do it. There's Fighting Styles already.<br /> <br /> <br /> In short - there are lots and lots of options out there already for defense and gun masters. The key is that they're options and you have to pick/build towards it - not all demons are super combatants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-16T14:02:02-07:00","id":171009,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I won't house rule then until I run RAW","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/354-pencilboy99","name":"PencilBoy99","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}